 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, `ATTEMPTS` in `larder/capture.py`. Each retry
+waits longer than the one before: 2, 4, 6, then 8 seconds, so a member can wait up to 20 seconds on the confirmation
+page.
+
+There used to be 3 attempts, sent back to back within a second. The card gateway answers slowly every Friday from
+17:00 to 19:00, its peak, so all three attempts landed in the same slow minute. One Friday, 58 pantry orders were
+confirmed but never charged, and a payments volunteer captured them by hand from the gateway's dashboard the next
+morning. Switching gateways was not possible because the contract runs to December 2026. A replay of that Friday's
+timeouts against the gateway's sandbox showed that 5 attempts spaced 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds apart would have charged
+57 of the 58 orders. The maintainers decided the extra wait on the confirmation page was a fair price for not
+capturing orders by hand ([issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md)).
 
